==English==
{{wikipedia|Prosthesis|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|la|en}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|πρόσθεσις||addition|sc=polytonic|tr=prosthesis|lang=grc}}, from {{term|προστίθημι||I add|sc=polytonic|tr=prostithēmi|lang=grc}}, from {{term|πρός||towards|sc=polytonic|tr=pros|lang=grc}} + {{term|τίθημι||I place|sc=polytonic|tr=tithēmi|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|prostheses}}

# {{context|medicine|lang=en}} An artificial [[replacement]] for a body part, either internal or external.
# {{context|linguistics|prosody|lang=en}} [[prothesis]]

